+      "ragdoll": { "physicsAsset": "/Game/Characters/Mannequins/Rigs/PA_Mannequin.PA_Mannequin", "bone": 330, "boneHead": 480, "carry": 110, "carryHead": 140, "blast": 650, "blastUp": 320, "maxSpeed": 900, "settleSpeed": 18, "settleFor": 0.5, "minSim": 1.2, "maxSim": 5.0, "poolFade": 2.5, "linearDamping": 0.15, "angularDamping": 0.6, "startsPerFrame": 2, "maxUp": 250, "note": "AMIGoon death pass: the killing hit makes the body a ragdoll on the mannequin skeleton's physics asset (bodies collide with world geometry only: never the player, rounds, other bodies, the camera or sight lines). Changes of speed in cm/s: bone = the bone hit (boneHead for a head shot), carry = the whole body along the shot, blast = away from the explosion plus blastUp. At rest (pelvis under settleSpeed cm/s for settleFor s, after minSim s, at most maxSim s) the body is frozen where it lies and a pool spreads under it; the pool fades over poolFade s when the rules remove the body. No part of a falling body goes faster than maxSpeed or rises faster than maxUp cm/s (a blast: 1.5 x blastUp), so a body started against a wall or a ledge is not thrown. At most startsPerFrame ragdolls start in one frame (more deaths in that frame fall one frame later each: the start makes 22 bodies). Without the physics asset the death clip by direction plays instead. Presentation only" },
